---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/v2/BaseLayout.astro';
import NewsletterBlock from '../../../components/v2/NewsletterBlock.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + '/';

const driveTimes = [
  { from: 'Melbourne CBD', to: 'Mornington', time: '60 min' },
  { from: 'Melbourne CBD', to: 'Dromana', time: '75 min' },
  { from: 'Melbourne CBD', to: 'Rye', time: '90 min' },
  { from: 'Melbourne CBD', to: 'Sorrento', time: '95 min' },
  { from: 'Melbourne CBD', to: 'Portsea', time: '100 min' },
  { from: 'Melbourne CBD', to: 'Cape Schanck', time: '100 min' },
  { from: 'Melbourne CBD', to: 'Red Hill', time: '90 min' },
  { from: 'Melbourne CBD', to: 'Flinders', time: '105 min' },
  { from: 'Melbourne Airport', to: 'Mornington', time: '75 min' },
  { from: 'Melbourne Airport', to: 'Sorrento', time: '110 min' },
  { from: 'Queenscliff (via ferry)', to: 'Sorrento', time: '40 min ferry' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Getting to the Mornington Peninsula — Peninsula Insider"
  description="How to get to the Mornington Peninsula — freeway, airport, ferry, public transport, and drive times to every Peninsula town."
  section="explore"
  ogImage="/images/sourced/explore-hub-hero-01.webp"
>

  <section class="hero" aria-label="Getting here cover">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero__frame">
        <div class="hero__above">
          <div class="hero__meta">
            <a href={`${base}explore/`} class="hero__meta-tag" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">Explore</a>
            <span class="hero__meta-divider"></span>
            <span class="hero__meta-date">Transport</span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="hero__headline">Getting to the Peninsula.</h1>
          <p class="hero__dek">Ninety minutes from Melbourne CBD on a clear day. Forty by ferry from Queenscliff. This is how to arrive — freeway, airport, public transport — without turning the drive into the first problem of the weekend.</p>
        </div>
        <figure>
          <img class="hero__image" src={`${base}images/sourced/explore-hub-hero-01.webp`} alt="Peninsula" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">
          <figcaption class="hero__image-cap">
            <span>Peninsula approach</span>
            <span>Photography <span class="ornament">/</span> The Insider</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="letter">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="letter__frame" style="display:block;">
        <div class="letter__eyebrow">
          <span class="letter__eyebrow-rule"></span>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">From Melbourne</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="letter__head">The freeway route.</h2>
        <div class="letter__prose">
          <p>The standard route is the M3 Eastlink to the M11 Peninsula Link, joining the Mornington Peninsula Freeway (M11) southbound. The freeway serves the Peninsula's spine — exits for Mornington, Mount Martha, Dromana, Rosebud, Rye, Sorrento and Portsea are well-signed. From CBD to Mornington is typically 60 minutes, to Sorrento 95 minutes. Summer Saturday mornings add 30–45 minutes; leave before 9am or after 2pm to avoid the worst.</p>
          <p>For Red Hill, Main Ridge, Merricks and Flinders, exit at Dromana and take the Arthurs Seat Road up onto the plateau. The drive up the hill is part of the arrival experience — do not rush it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="letter">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="letter__frame" style="display:block;">
        <div class="letter__eyebrow">
          <span class="letter__eyebrow-rule"></span>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">From Geelong / Great Ocean Road</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="letter__head">The Sorrento–Queenscliff ferry.</h2>
        <div class="letter__prose">
          <p>The car ferry runs every hour each way between Sorrento and Queenscliff. 40 minutes across Port Phillip Bay. Useful in two ways: as a scenic alternative to driving around Melbourne (saves about 90 minutes from Geelong to Sorrento), and as a way to combine a Peninsula weekend with a Great Ocean Road week. The ferry takes cars, caravans, bikes and foot passengers. Book ahead in peak season. <a href="https://www.searoad.com.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">searoad.com.au</a> for schedules.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="letter">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="letter__frame" style="display:block;">
        <div class="letter__eyebrow">
          <span class="letter__eyebrow-rule"></span>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">From Melbourne Airport</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="letter__head">Airport to Peninsula.</h2>
        <div class="letter__prose">
          <p>Melbourne Tullamarine to Mornington is 75 minutes, to Sorrento 110 minutes, via the CityLink and EastLink–Peninsula Link corridor. There is no direct airport bus to the Peninsula — you need a car or a private transfer. SkyBus to Southern Cross Station plus a V/Line coach is possible but slow; for international visitors, renting a car at the airport is the practical choice.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="letter">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="letter__frame" style="display:block;">
        <div class="letter__eyebrow">
          <span class="letter__eyebrow-rule"></span>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">Public transport</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="letter__head">Train and coach.</h2>
        <div class="letter__prose">
          <p>Metro train from Flinders Street Station to Frankston (50 min). From Frankston, V/Line coach services connect to major Peninsula towns — Mornington, Dromana, Rosebud, Rye, Sorrento and Portsea. Services are infrequent compared to Melbourne routes; verify timetable before committing to public transport. The Peninsula is genuinely difficult to navigate without a car once you arrive; public transport works for a focused single-town base (Sorrento is the strongest option), not for a touring weekend.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="letter">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="letter__frame" style="display:block;">
        <div class="letter__eyebrow">
          <span class="letter__eyebrow-rule"></span>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">Drive times</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="letter__head">From where to where.</h2>
        <div class="letter__prose">
          <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-family:var(--sans,'Inter'),sans-serif; font-size:.95rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr style="border-bottom:2px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
                <th style="text-align:left; padding:.6rem 0;">From</th>
                <th style="text-align:left; padding:.6rem 0;">To</th>
                <th style="text-align:left; padding:.6rem 0;">Time</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {driveTimes.map(row => (
                <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
                  <td style="padding:.6rem 0;">{row.from}</td>
                  <td style="padding:.6rem 0;">{row.to}</td>
                  <td style="padding:.6rem 0;">{row.time}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem;">Times assume non-peak traffic. Summer Saturday mornings from Melbourne add 30–45 minutes; returning on summer Sunday evenings can add 30 minutes. The freeway flows well outside those windows.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NewsletterBlock />

</BaseLayout>
